$XY$ is tangent to a circle at $P$. The points $A$, $B$ and $P$ lie on the circle, with $\angle BPX=48^{\circ}$. Find $\angle PAB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (P) at (0,-2);
\coordinate (A) at (160:2);
\coordinate (B) at (6:2);
\coordinate (X) at (2.7,-2);
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (-2.7,-2) node[left] {$Y$} -- (X) node[right] {$X$};
\draw (P) -- (A) -- (B) -- cycle;
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\pic[draw,"$48^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=X--P--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$XY$ is tangent to a circle at $P$. The points $A$, $B$ and $P$ lie on the circle. Given $\angle PBA=46^{\circ}$ and $\angle BPX=72^{\circ}$, find $\angle PAB$, $\angle APY$ and $\angle APB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (P) at (0,-2);
\coordinate (A) at (178:2);
\coordinate (B) at (54:2);
\coordinate (X) at (2.7,-2);
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (-2.7,-2) node[left] {$Y$} -- (X) node[right] {$X$};
\draw (P) -- (A) -- (B) -- cycle;
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\pic[draw,"$72^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=X--P--B};
\pic[draw,"$46^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=A--B--P};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$XY$ is tangent to a circle at $P$. The points $A$, $B$ and $P$ lie on the circle, with $AP=AB$ and $\angle PAB=76^{\circ}$. Find $\angle APY$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,decorations.markings}
\tikzset{equal side/.style={postaction={decorate},decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0,-3pt)--(0,3pt);}}}}
\coordinate (P) at (0,-2);
\coordinate (A) at (166:2);
\coordinate (B) at (62:2);
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (-2.7,-2) node[left] {$Y$} -- (2.7,-2) node[right] {$X$};
\draw[equal side] (A)--(P);
\draw[equal side] (A)--(B);
\draw (P)--(B);
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\pic[draw,"$76^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=P--A--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PQ$ is tangent to a circle at $C$. The points $A$, $B$ and $C$ lie on the circle, and $O$ is its centre. Join $OC$ and $OB$. Let $\angle BCQ=x$. Prove that $\angle BCQ=\angle CAB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0,-2);
\coordinate (A) at (150:2);
\coordinate (B) at (20:2);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.7,-2);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\draw (-2.7,-2) node[left] {$P$} -- (Q) node[right] {$Q$};
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (C)--(O)--(B);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[below] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\pic[draw,"$x$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=Q--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$XY$ is tangent to a circle at $P$. Chord $PB$ forms the marked $54^{\circ}$ angle with $PX$. Points $A$ and $D$ lie on opposite sides of chord $PB$. Which angle, $\angle PAB$ or $\angle PDB$, equals the marked angle? State its size.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (P) at (0,-2);
\coordinate (B) at (18:2);
\coordinate (A) at (150:2);
\coordinate (D) at (-36:2);
\coordinate (X) at (2.7,-2);
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (-2.7,-2) node[left] {$Y$} -- (X) node[right] {$X$};
\draw (P)--(B);
\draw (P)--(A)--(B);
\draw (P)--(D)--(B);
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (D) {$D$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.55cm] {angle=X--P--B};
\node at (1.10,-0.98) {$54^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
